source:
\begin{proof}
Suppose $z \in [x]$ and $x \nsless y$. Then $z \nsless u$ for all $u
\in [y]$. If $z \in [y]$, we would have $z \nsless z$. Similarly if $y
\nsless x$.
\end{proof}

