  \end{align*}
  where $\Gamma$ is again a list of variables indexed from zero, and
  $\Gamma[n]$ denotes the variable in position~$n$. For example,
  if $\Gamma$ is $x,y,z$, then $\Gamma[1]$ is $y$.

