\begin{defn}[Extensionality]
  We extend the equivalence relation $\equal$ with the (\ext) rule:
  \begin{center}
  If $Mx \equal Nx$ then $M \equal N$, provided $x \notin FV(MN)$.
  \end{center}
  and denote the extended relation as $\equal[\ext]$.
\end{defn}

